            <ArticleTitle>[3H]imipramine binding sites are decreased in platelets of chronic pain patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tritiated imipramine binding to whole platelets was measured in 16 chronic pain patients not suffering from major depression and in a control group. Maximum binding was significantly lower in chronic pain patients than in the control group, whereas the binding affinity was not significantly different.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
